# Dev-stack vault wiring (committed — every value here is a toy).
#
# The dev Vault runs in **dev mode**: in-memory, auto-unsealed, with a
# known root token. That is exactly what you want for `docker compose up`
# and exactly what you must not run for a customer. The core and runner
# authenticate with the root token here instead of AppRole, because the
# alternative is a seed step every developer has to run before the stack
# starts, and a stack that does not start on the first command is a stack
# people work around.
#
# The pilot and any real deployment use AppRole instead — see
# deploy/vault-seed.sh and .secrets/vault.env. The only difference is
# these three lines; nothing in the core or the runner changes.
VAULT_ADDR=http://vault:8200
VAULT_TOKEN=dev-root-token
